/// A STOCK: one row per claim per month end that the claim was still outstanding - 670,151 rows across 47 month ends. This is what makes an ageing possible at all, because a receivable's age is a property of a date, not of the claim. Carried at the allowed amount and aged from the submission date, which is the clock a payer is held to.
